AIM:To write a Python program to demonstrate various tuple operations, such as accessing elements, finding length, counting and indexing elements, finding maximum/minimum values, calculating the sum, checking membership, and converting between tuples and lists.

Algorithm
1.Start the program.

2.Create a tuple t = (10, 20, 30, 40).

3.Display the tuple.

4.Access and display the first element using t[0].

5.Access and display the last element using t[-1].

6.Find and display the length of the tuple using len().

7.Count the occurrence of 20 using count().

8.Find the index of 30 using index().

9.Find and display the maximum value using max().

10.Find and display the minimum value using min().

11.Calculate and display the sum of all elements using sum().

12.Check whether 40 is present in the tuple using the in operator.

13.Convert the tuple into a list using list().

14.Convert the list back into a tuple using tuple().

15.Display the converted list and tuple.

16.Stop the program.


t = (10,20,30,40)
print("tuple:",t)
print("first element:",t[0])
print("last element;",t[-1])

print("length:",len(t))

print("count of 20:",t.count(20))

print("index of 30:",t.index(30))

print("maximum:",max(t))
print("minimum:",min(t))
print("sum:",sum(t))
print("is 40 present?",40 in t)

l = list(t)
print("tuple converted to list:", l)

t2 = tuple(l)
print("list converted to tuple:", t2)

